## Context

Split from [[1702]], whose original subject this slice keeps: matching
judgements as calibrated stances with a cutoff per result (author decisions
of 2026-09-30, recorded on 1702), plus the M3b targets for observations,
assets, parties and crosswalks. Normative text: the accepted specification
v1 (tag `jetp-spec-v1`), `docs/jetp-fusion.md` §§ 1 to 6, `docs/jetp-results.md`
§ 3 (two match thresholds), `docs/jetp-extraction.md` § 11, storage contract
`docs/jetp-ledger-storage.md` § 1 and § 4.

Blocked by [[1870]], which carries the shared columns (stance, likelihood,
confidence, basis, `recorded_at`, `run_id`) and migrates the same DDL.
Reconciliation with CRS and IATI ([[0721]]) and the join to assets
([[0723]]) build on this slice.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The `matching.panel` rule emits a stance, an IPCC likelihood term and an IPCC confidence level on every matching judgement (the columns are [[1870]])
- [ ] Every derived result declares its matching cutoff in its run record, and the observatory's counts are produced at that cutoff; figures at the current default are unchanged or each change is explained
- [ ] Counting scopes are stored apart from publisher-stated perimeters, and nothing in the build reads the World Bank pool as a perimeter
- [ ] `assets.operator_party_id` is dropped, and the `party_in` term's range covers agreement, project and asset with the Party roles as its closed list (W1-32)
- [ ] `party-names` carries a `preferred` flag, the form type `preferred` is retired from the terms in force, and the validator keeps exactly one preferred form in force per party (W1-33)
- [ ] `adjudications.decision_type` accepts `revision` and `preference` as terms in force, with their member roles (W1-38)
- [ ] `status-crosswalk` and `sector-crosswalk` carry `mapping_relation`, required on accepted rows (W1-64)
- [ ] The validator refuses a `same_as` chain between referents deeper than one (W1-31)
- [ ] The as-of builder applies a named correction overlay (storage contract § 1) for a correction release (W1-36)
- [ ] `observations` carries `own_status_axis` and `missing_reason` (a closed `terms` list) (W2-56)
- [ ] `projects.aliases` is dropped; a project's other names are read from the labels of its attached lines (X-22)
- [ ] The storage contract § 1 and § 4 describe what the code does for the tables of this slice
- [ ] `make jetp-ledger-check`, `make check-fast`, `make lint` and `make check-domain-jetp` pass
